# Multi Ports Manager - Project Structure Guide

This is a TypeScript-based CLI tool for managing multiple project ports. The main entry point is [src/bin/muti-ports.ts](mdc:src/bin/muti-ports.ts), which serves as the CLI interface.

## Core Architecture

- **Entry Point**: [src/index.ts](mdc:src/index.ts) - Main application logic
- **CLI Interface**: [src/bin/muti-ports.ts](mdc:src/bin/muti-ports.ts) - Command-line interface using Commander.js
- **Core Managers**:
  - [src/manager.ts](mdc:src/manager.ts) - Main manager orchestrating all operations
  - [src/project-manager.ts](mdc:src/project-manager.ts) - Handles project CRUD operations
  - [src/port-manager.ts](mdc:src/port-manager.ts) - Manages port allocation and checking
  - [src/env-manager.ts](mdc:src/env-manager.ts) - Handles .env file operations
- **Internationalization**: [src/i18n/index.ts](mdc:src/i18n/index.ts) - Multi-language support (EN/CN)
- **Type Definitions**: [src/types.ts](mdc:src/types.ts) - TypeScript interfaces and types

## Build & Configuration

- **TypeScript Config**: [tsconfig.json](mdc:tsconfig.json) - TypeScript compilation settings
- **Package Config**: [package.json](mdc:package.json) - Dependencies and build scripts
- **Build Output**: Compiled JavaScript goes to `dist/` directory

## Key Dependencies

- **Commander.js**: CLI framework
- **Chalk**: Terminal colorization
- **Inquirer**: Interactive prompts
- **Portfinder**: Port availability detection
- **PS List**: Process management
- **Dotenv**: Environment variable handling
